<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Shown as the final ("conclusion") screen of the macOS installer. build_release_package.sh
     substitutes <fastsurfer> with FastSurfer<version> and copies the result into the installer
     resources; edit_distribution.py registers it as text/html, so the links below are clickable.
     Keep it short: the pane is narrow and scrolling is easy to miss. -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body {
    font: 13px -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 2px 4px 12px;
  }
  h2 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 3px; }
  p, ul { margin: 3px 0; }
  ul { padding-left: 17px; }
  pre {
    background: rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.14);
    border-radius: 5px;
    font: 11px ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
    margin: 5px 0;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  code { font: 11px ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .muted { opacity: 0.75; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<p><b>FastSurfer is installed in /Applications/<fastsurfer></b></p>

<h2>Open the FastSurfer console</h2>
<p>Double-click <b><fastsurfer></b> in your Applications folder. It opens a Terminal window that
has everything set up &mdash; the Python environment, the pruned FreeSurfer bundled with this
package, and <code>run_fastsurfer.sh</code> on your <code>PATH</code>. You can recognize it by the
<code>(<fastsurfer>)</code> prefix in the prompt.</p>
<p class="muted">Afterwards any Terminal window works too: run
<code>source macos_setup_fastsurfer.sh</code>.</p>

<h2>Run FastSurfer</h2>
<p>Segmentation only (no FreeSurfer license needed):</p>
<pre>run_fastsurfer.sh --seg_only --device mps \
  --sd &lt;output/dir&gt; --sid &lt;subject_id&gt; --t1 &lt;subject/t1.nii.gz&gt;</pre>
<p>Full pipeline, including surfaces:</p>
<pre>run_fastsurfer.sh --device mps --fs_license ~/fs_license.txt \
  --sd &lt;output/dir&gt; --sid &lt;subject_id&gt; --t1 &lt;subject/t1.nii.gz&gt;</pre>
<p class="muted"><code>--device mps</code> uses the GPU of Apple silicon Macs and is roughly twice
as fast as <code>--device cpu</code>.</p>

<h2>FreeSurfer license</h2>
<p>The surface pipeline (and <code>--tal_reg</code> for eTIV) needs a free FreeSurfer license:
<a href="https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/registration.html">register here</a>, then save the
license file in your home directory and pass it with <code>--fs_license</code>. It cannot be stored
inside the bundled FreeSurfer, which this installer wrote as <code>root</code>.</p>

<h2>Documentation</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="https://deep-mi.org/FastSurfer/stable/overview/INSTALL.html#macos">macOS installation and usage</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://deep-mi.org/FastSurfer/stable/">FastSurfer documentation</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://github.com/Deep-MI/FastSurfer/issues">Report a problem</a></li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>
